    "q-152901": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152901",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}, & -1<x<0, \\\\ {x}^{2}, & 0\\le x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(0+1)+\\frac{1}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{45}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
