    "q-152900": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152900",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}\\,{x}^{3}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}\\,{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{7}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
