    "q-152921": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152921",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & 1<x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{5}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fifth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{5}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{5}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}\\cdot (1-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{5}-{x}^{8})\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6}\\,{x}^{6}-\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{9}){|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{24}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{9}-0)+\\frac{1}{24}(64-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{21}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{193}{72}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
