    "q-131143": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131143",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,0<x<3\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5]=2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-5\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=3$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5] & =2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-5 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
